From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mediacodec: request the opaque output after parsing the codec
 configuration

The opaque output was requested before the extra data was parsed. An H.264
or HEVC input that declares no aspect therefore started its output at a
provisional 1:1, and the input's track format took that value too. The SPS
aspect (0009) arrived only with MediaCodec's output format update, which can
reach the window after the first picture: a frame read as soon as it arrives
was then shaped by the provisional 1:1.

Parse the codec configuration first, so an output whose SPS is in the extra
data starts with that aspect. Inputs whose parameter sets arrive in band keep
the previous behaviour.
---
diff --git a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
index 5dbf1f4..f886e9b 100644
--- a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
+++ b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
@@ -792,12 +792,8 @@ static int OpenDecoder(vlc_object_t *p_this, pf_MediaCodecApi_init pf_init)
                 p_dec->fmt_out.video.i_width = p_sys->video.i_visible_width;
             if (p_sys->video.i_visible_height > 0)
                 p_dec->fmt_out.video.i_height = p_sys->video.i_visible_height;
-
-            if (UpdateVout(p_dec) != VLC_SUCCESS)
-            {
-                msg_Err(p_dec, "Opaque Vout request failed");
-                goto bailout;
-            }
+            /* The opaque Vout is requested below, once the codec
+             * configuration is parsed. */
         }
     }
     else
@@ -836,6 +832,18 @@ static int OpenDecoder(vlc_object_t *p_this, pf_MediaCodecApi_init pf_init)
         }
     }
 
+    /* Request the opaque Vout after the codec configuration is parsed: an
+     * H.264/HEVC input that declares no aspect then starts its output with
+     * the SAR of the SPS in its extra data, rather than with a provisional
+     * 1:1 that is only corrected once MediaCodec reports its output format,
+     * which can be after the first picture reached the surface. */
+    if (p_dec->fmt_out.i_codec == VLC_CODEC_ANDROID_OPAQUE
+     && UpdateVout(p_dec) != VLC_SUCCESS)
+    {
+        msg_Err(p_dec, "Opaque Vout request failed");
+        goto bailout;
+    }
+
     i_ret = StartMediaCodec(p_dec);
     if (i_ret != VLC_SUCCESS)
     {
